Secondary sandbox issues seen on this run (worked around, not fatal):
  * the repo mount is delete-restricted — `rm` returns EPERM, `mv` works. Git's
    index.lock therefore has to be renamed away between operations, and the
    pre-migration proofing debris could only be untracked (git rm --cached) and
    gitignored, not deleted. Stray .git/lk.* and .git/index.lock.*.bak files are
    harmless leftovers of that workaround; delete them on a local checkout.
